{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c9c2def2-aa05-4d26-ae10-4b589f2e3dd3","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Choose two endpoints on a circle and a vertex on the opposite arc. The two chords form an inscribed angle.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"Inscribed angle theorem"},{"op":"figure","id":"circlefig","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-3.8,3.8],"y":[-3.8,3.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"circ","center":[0,0],"r":3},{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[-2.598076211,-1.5],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[2.598076211,-1.5],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":[0,3],"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"a"}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"b"}},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"p"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.2,"label":"α"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c9c2def2-aa05-4d26-ae10-4b589f2e3dd3","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The central angle and inscribed angle intercept the same arc AB. The inscribed angle is half the central angle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"central","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"o","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"o"},"to":{"at":"a"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"o"},"to":{"at":"b"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"o"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.25,"label":"θ"},{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"o"},"r":3,"start":210,"end":330,"label":"arc AB"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"theorem","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\alpha=\\frac{\\theta}{2}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c9c2def2-aa05-4d26-ae10-4b589f2e3dd3","step":{"id":"s3","script":"For example, a central angle of 120 degrees gives an inscribed angle of 60 degrees, wherever P lies on the opposite arc.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"values","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0,-1.15],"text":"120°"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,1.95],"text":"60°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"theorem","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\angle APB=\\frac{120^\\circ}{2}=60^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the central angle intercepting arc AB is 100°, what is the inscribed angle intercepting that same arc?","expected_gist":"50°, because the inscribed angle is half the central angle."}}}
